  "chapter": {
    "number": 74,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(75) For the end, Destroy not, a Psalm of a Song for Asaph."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "We will give thanks to you, O God, we will give thanks, and call upon your name: I will declare all your wonderful works.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When I shall take a set time, I will judge righteously.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The earth is dissolved, and all that dwell in it: I have strengthened its pillars. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I said to the transgressors, Do not transgress; and to the sinners, Lift not up the horn.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Lift not up your horn on high; speak not unrighteousness against God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For good comes neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the desert mountains.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For God is the judge; he puts down one, and raises up another.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there is a cup in the hand of the Lord, full of unmingled wine; and he has",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 137
          },
          {
            "text": "turned it from side to side, but its dregs have not been wholly poured out; all the sinners of the earth shall drink them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I will exult for ever: I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I will break all the horns of sinners; but the horns of the righteous one shall be exalted.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 137,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. from this into that.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 74,
          "verse": 8
        }
      }
    ]
  },
